ory":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, October to November came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, more than any other pair since 1951. It is also the driest pair at 6.28 inches of normal, and in 2025 it ran 60% of normal on the middle. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 42% of normal on the middle while May to June shows 130%. Grid 17594 had its driest year in 2007 at 59% of normal.</p>"}
